    # ...
    # Year k: Alien k becomes adult. Aliens 1, 2, ..., k-1 are adults.
    
    # Let S be the number of adults who have at least one stone.
    # When alien k becomes an adult:
    # 1. b[k-1] += S
    # 2. For all j < k-1, if b[j] > 0, b[j] -= 1.
    # 3. Alien k-1 is now an adult. If b[k-1] > 0, S increases.
    #    Wait, the logic is slightly different:
    #    At year k, alien k becomes an adult. 
    #    The adults are 1, 2, ..., k-1.
    #    Let count be the number of j in {1, ..., k-1} such that b[j-1] > 0.
    #    b[k-1] = b[k-1] + count.
    #    Then, for all j in {1, ..., k-1}, if b[j-1] > 0, b[j-1] = b[j-1] - 1.
    
    # This looks like we can maintain the count of adults with stones.
